The Central Bank expects firms to plan how they would exit an outsourcing arrangement in the following situations:
a) Failure on the part of the OSP to provide the service to the requisite standard;
b) Unexpected termination of the arrangement dictated by the OSP/CSP;
c) Stressed circumstances on the part of the OSP such as hostile takeover, insolvency or liquidation;
d) Any other circumstance that the regulated firm envisages may prompt it to exit the arrangement. [1]

